ate_rev_volatility":0.10306242879645164,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.8,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.06650948526075516,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.17888444515185697,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.02854578441111255,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0671871648265937,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":85.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.005347597816763305,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":56.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.1128795976483038,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00821,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Lazard, Inc. operates as a financial advisory and asset management firm in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company operates through two segments, Financial Advisory and Asset Management. The Financial Advisory segment offers financial advisory services, such as mergers and acquisitions, capital markets, shareholder, sovereign, geopolitical, and other strategic advisory services, as well as restructuring and liability management, and capital raising and placement services. This segment offers its services to corporate, partnership, institutional, government, sovereign, and individual clients to various industry areas, including consumers and retail; financial institutions; financial sponsors; healthcare and life sciences; industrials; media, entertainment, and sports; power, energy, and infrastructure; real estate; technology; and telecom and digital infrastructure. The Asset Management segment offers a range of investment solutions; investment and wealth management services in equity and fixed income strategies; asset allocation strategies; and alternative investments and private equity funds to corporations, public funds, sovereign entities, endowments and foundations, labor funds, financial intermediaries, and private clients. It also provides primary fundraising, secondary advisory, and GP capital advisory services for private equity, private credit, infrastructure, and real estate markets. Lazard, Inc. was incorporated in 1848 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter R. Orszag | CEO & Chairman | Age 56 | Compensation: $5.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $948K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $145K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $107K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Lazard, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.1B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $487M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 25% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.25356680718236513},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (LAZ)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/139/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_LAZ_112526122601_1795584361.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795584361.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lazard Global Total Return and Income Fund Declares Monthly Distribution and Issues Estimated Sources of the Distribution Announced in October","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/lazard-global-total-return-and-income-fund-declares-monthly-distribution-and-issues-estimated-sources-of-the-distribution-announced-in-october-302949838.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795554900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Why is Lazard stock rocketing higher today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/laz/news/why-up-down/why-is-lazard-stock-rocketing-higher-today","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795456539.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lazard CFO Tracy Farr Acquires 477 RSUs via Dividend Reinvestment on November 13, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/lazard-cfo-tracy-farr-acquires-477-rsus-via-dividend-reinvestment-on-november-13-2026","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794956025.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","leadership","dividend"]},{"title":"Lazard COO Alexandra Soto Gains 3,814 RSUs via Dividend Equivalent Reinvestment on November 13, 2026","source":"kalkinemedi